 "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/design-add-and-search-words-data-structure/",
 "pattern": "Trie + DFS for wildcards",
 "statement": "Design a dictionary with `addWord(word)` and `search(word)`. In `search` the pattern may contain dots: each `.` matches **any single letter**.",
 "example": {
  "input": "WordDictionary()\naddWord('bad')\naddWord('dad')\nsearch('pad')  →  False\nsearch('.ad')  →  True\nsearch('b..')  →  True",
  "output": "",
  "why": "'.ad' matches bad (and dad); 'b..' matches bad; nothing stored starts with p."
 },
 "more": [
  {
   "input": "WordDictionary()\naddWord('bad')\naddWord('dad')\naddWord('mad')\nsearch('pad')  →  False\nsearch('bad')  →  True\nsearch('.ad')  →  True\nsearch('b..')  →  True\nsearch('b.')  →  False\nsearch('...')  →  True\nsearch('....')  →  False",
   "output": ""
  }
 ],
 "idea": [
  "Without dots this is exactly a trie: follow one branch per letter.",
  "A `.` can be any letter, so at that position we cannot know which branch to take — **try them all**.",
  "That is a depth-first search: for each child branch, recursively match the rest of the pattern. One success is enough; if every branch fails, the pattern does not match."
 ],
 "code": "class TrieNode:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.children = {}\n        self.is_end = False\n\nclass WordDictionary:\n    def __init__(self):\n        self.root = TrieNode()\n\n    def addWord(self, word: str) -> None:\n        node = self.root\n        for char in word:\n            if char not in node.children:\n                node.children[char] = TrieNode()\n            node = node.children[char]\n        node.is_end = True\n\n    def search(self, word: str) -> bool:\n        def dfs(start, node):\n            # Does word[start:] match some path that begins at `node`?\n            for i in range(start, len(word)):\n                char = word[i]\n                if char == \".\":\n                    for letter in node.children:\n                        if dfs(i + 1, node.children[letter]):\n                            return True\n                    return False\n                if char not in node.children:\n                    return False\n                node = node.children[char]\n            return node.is_end\n\n        return dfs(0, self.root)",
 "complexity": {
  "time": "O(L) to add, up to O(26ᴸ) to search",
  "timeWhy": "Adding follows one branch per letter. Each dot in a search can fan out to every child, though real dictionaries cut that down quickly.",
  "space": "O(total letters)",
  "spaceWhy": "The trie stores each distinct prefix once; the search recursion is at most L deep."
 },
